I need to go to sleep and wait for an interrupt to wake me up so 
I don't use up the cpu cycles. Here is what I do:

    If (operation not done yet) {
        EnableInterrupt;
        if (operation not done yet) {
            tsleep for 1 second;
	}
    }

I run into problem where the sleep times out very often which 
should never happen. I suspect that tsleep/sleep is not atomic
interrupt comes in after the sleep function call and before it 
actually goes to sleep. I tried to take out the 2nd check and go
to sleep immediately after enabling the interrupt but it doesn't 
help at all.

I can work around the problem by sleeping for 10 msec at a time 
in a loop and break out the loop if the operation is done but 
that not very efficient. Is there any way to do atomic sleep?

Thank you for any help.

